# Cute Cursive Design

Status: DONE
Milestone: M3 Local visual revision complete; final user acceptance pending
Dependencies: 04_VISUAL_DESIGN.todo, 06_TESTING_AND_LAUNCH.todo, 08_READABILITY_AND_SIMPLE_ORDERING.todo, 09_STORY_AND_CAKE_STICKERS.todo

## Purpose

Historical revision: the user subsequently rejected its palette change and
Dancing Script font. Workstream 11 restores the original colours and uses clearer
Courgette; the other cute layout details are retained. Do not restore this revision.

Respond to the user's explicit request for cursive fonts and an extremely cute
website without sacrificing readable content, faithful photos or simple ordering.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the prior site and review before changing its appearance.
- [x] Add unmodified upstream Dancing Script with its SIL Open Font License.
- [x] Use cursive display text and large cake names; keep DM Sans reading/actions.
- [x] Add blush/sage/cream colours, rose pills, scallops and heart/bow doodles.
- [x] Keep restored story, all five stickers and direct contact unchanged.
- [x] Update sharing artwork to match the cursive/sticker treatment.
- [x] Support enlarged text through wrapping and responsive tracks, not smaller text.
- [x] Run local checks and inspect actual browser/sharing-image output.
- [x] Leave branding unchanged until the user selects a proposed name.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The locally hosted cursive face actually loads in the browser.
- [x] Display headings, wordmark, note and cake names use Dancing Script.
- [x] Body and order actions stay clear, with 18px copy/16px labels/48px controls.
- [x] No page overflow at six standard widths or 200% text at 320/390/600/1280px.
- [x] Focus, skip link, no-JavaScript contact, reduced motion and photo viewer remain.
- [x] Generated output excludes masks, sources, model files and private artifacts.
- [x] Final appearance approval and public deployment remain separate.

